{
  "schema_version": "1.0.0",
  "edition_id": "WEBSTER1833",
  "book_code": "PSA",
  "chapter": 89,
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "PSA.89.1",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.89.1",
      "verse": 1,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Maschil of Ethan the Ezrahite. I will sing of the mercies of the LORD for ever: with my mouth will I make known thy faithfulness to all generations.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.89.2",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.89.2",
      "verse": 2,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For I have said, Mercy shall be built up for ever: thy faithfulness wilt thou establish in the very heavens.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.89.3",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.89.3",
      "verse": 3,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "I have made a covenant with my chosen, I have sworn to David my servant,",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.89.4",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.89.4",
      "verse": 4,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Thy seed will I establish for ever, and build up thy throne to all generations. Selah.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.89.5",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.89.5",
      "verse": 5,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And the heavens shall praise thy wonders, O LORD; thy faithfulness also in the congregation of the saints.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.89.6",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.89.6",
      "verse": 6,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For who in the heaven can be compared to the LORD? ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "who",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " among the sons of the mighty can be likened to the LORD?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.89.7",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.89.7",
      "verse": 7,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "God is greatly to be feared in the assembly of the saints, and to be had in reverence by all ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "them that are",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " about him.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.89.8",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.89.8",
      "verse": 8,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "O LORD God of hosts, who ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " a strong LORD like to thee? or to thy faithfulness around thee?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.89.9",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.89.9",
      "verse": 9,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Thou rulest the raging of the sea: when its waves arise, thou stillest them.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.89.10",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.89.10",
      "verse": 10,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Thou hast broken Rahab in pieces, as one that is slain; thou hast scattered thy enemies with thy strong arm.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.89.11",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.89.11",
      "verse": 11,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The heavens ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "are",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " thine, the earth also ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " thine: ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "as for",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " the world, and the fullness of it, thou hast founded them.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.89.12",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.89.12",
      "verse": 12,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The north and the south thou hast created them: Tabor and Hermon shall rejoice in thy name.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.89.13",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.89.13",
      "verse": 13,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Thou hast a mighty arm: strong is thy hand, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "and",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " high is thy right hand.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.89.14",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.89.14",
      "verse": 14,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Justice and judgment ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "are",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " the habitation of thy throne: mercy and truth shall go before thy face.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.89.15",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.89.15",
      "verse": 15,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Blessed ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "are",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " the people that know the joyful sound: they shall walk, O LORD, in the light of thy countenance.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.89.16",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.89.16",
      "verse": 16,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "In thy name shall they rejoice all the day: and in thy righteousness shall they be exalted.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.89.17",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.89.17",
      "verse": 17,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For thou ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "art",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " the glory of their strength: and in thy favor our horn shall be exalted.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.89.18",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.89.18",
      "verse": 18,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For the LORD ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " our defense; and the Holy One of Israel ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " our king.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.89.19",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.89.19",
      "verse": 19,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Then thou didst speak in vision to thy holy one, and say, I have laid help upon ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "one that is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " mighty; I have exalted ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "one",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " chosen out of the people.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.89.20",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.89.20",
      "verse": 20,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "I have found David my servant; with my holy oil have I anointed him:",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.89.21",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.89.21",
      "verse": 21,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "With whom my hand shall be established: my arm also shall strengthen him.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.89.22",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.89.22",
      "verse": 22,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The enemy shall not exact upon him; nor the son of wickedness afflict him.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.89.23",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.89.23",
      "verse": 23,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And I will beat down his foes before his face, and afflict them that hate him.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.89.24",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.89.24",
      "verse": 24,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "But my faithfulness and my mercy ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "shall be",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " with him: and in my name shall his horn be exalted.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.89.25",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.89.25",
      "verse": 25,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "I will set his hand also in the sea, and his right hand in the rivers.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.89.26",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.89.26",
      "verse": 26,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "He shall cry to me, Thou ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "art",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " my father, my God, and the rock of my salvation.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.89.27",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.89.27",
      "verse": 27,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Also I will make him ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "my",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " first-born, higher than the kings of the earth.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.89.28",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.89.28",
      "verse": 28,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "My mercy will I keep for him for evermore, and my covenant shall stand fast with him.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.89.29",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.89.29",
      "verse": 29,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "His seed also will I make ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "to endure",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " for ever, and his throne as the days of heaven.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.89.30",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.89.30",
      "verse": 30,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "If his children forsake my law, and walk not in my judgments;",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.89.31",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.89.31",
      "verse": 31,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "If they break my statutes, and keep not my commandments;",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.89.32",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.89.32",
      "verse": 32,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Then will I visit their transgression with the rod, and their iniquity with stripes.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.89.33",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.89.33",
      "verse": 33,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Nevertheless my loving-kindness will I not utterly take from him, nor suffer my faithfulness to fail.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.89.34",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.89.34",
      "verse": 34,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "My covenant will I not break, nor alter the thing that hath gone out of my lips.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.89.35",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.89.35",
      "verse": 35,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Once have I sworn by my holiness that I will not lie to David.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.89.36",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.89.36",
      "verse": 36,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "His seed shall endure for ever, and his throne as the sun before me.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.89.37",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.89.37",
      "verse": 37,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "It shall be established for ever as the moon, and ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "as",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " a faithful witness in heaven. Selah.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.89.38",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.89.38",
      "verse": 38,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "But thou hast cast off and abhorred, thou hast been wroth with thy anointed.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.89.39",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.89.39",
      "verse": 39,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Thou hast made void the covenant of thy servant: thou hast profaned his crown ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "by casting it",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " to the ground.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.89.40",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.89.40",
      "verse": 40,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Thou hast broken down all his hedges; thou hast brought his strong holds to ruin.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.89.41",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.89.41",
      "verse": 41,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "All that pass by the way plunder him: he is a reproach to his neighbors.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.89.42",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.89.42",
      "verse": 42,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Thou hast set up the right hand of his adversaries; thou hast made all his enemies to rejoice.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.89.43",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.89.43",
      "verse": 43,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Thou hast also turned the edge of his sword, and hast not made him to stand in the battle.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.89.44",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.89.44",
      "verse": 44,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Thou hast made his glory to cease, and cast his throne down to the ground.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.89.45",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.89.45",
      "verse": 45,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The days of his youth hast thou shortened: thou hast covered him with shame. Selah.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.89.46",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.89.46",
      "verse": 46,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "How long, LORD, wilt thou hide thyself? for ever? shall thy wrath burn like fire?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.89.47",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.89.47",
      "verse": 47,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Remember how short my time is: why hast thou made all men in vain?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.89.48",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.89.48",
      "verse": 48,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "What man ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is he that",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " liveth, and shall not see death? shall he deliver his soul from the hand of the grave? Selah.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.89.49",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.89.49",
      "verse": 49,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "LORD, where ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "are",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " thy former loving-kindnesses, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "which",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " thou didst swear to David in thy truth?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.89.50",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.89.50",
      "verse": 50,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Remember, LORD, the reproach of thy servants; ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "how",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " I do bear in my bosom ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "the reproach of",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " all the mighty people;",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.89.51",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.89.51",
      "verse": 51,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "With which thy enemies have reproached, O LORD; with which they have reproached the footsteps of thy anointed",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.89.52",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.89.52",
      "verse": 52,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Blessed ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "be",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " the LORD for evermore. Amen and amen.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    }
  ]
}
